      <section>
        <h2><span class="pin-name">01</span> The context</h2>
        <p>
          UrbanLoop is a transport project based on autonomous capsules that run on loops. TÉLÉCOM Nancy owns a
          small-scale model of it, used as a demonstrator and for embedded systems lab sessions. Its rails and
          capsules had been rebuilt in 2023: this new version had to be made usable.
        </p>
        <p>
          The internship, in a pair with another intern: bring back the features of the previous version,
          improve the monitoring and program the switch logic.
        </p>
        <h3>What the model is made of</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><b>Two loops</b> running in opposite directions, joined by <b>two switches</b> (101 and 102), each one driven by an ESP32 and moved by a stepper motor.</li>
          <li><b>Two capsules</b>, with distance sensors to keep their spacing and rear LEDs that signal a capsule detected ahead of them, or their direction at a switch. They continuously transmit their ID and destination over infrared (IrDA).</li>
          <li><b>Two stations</b> (141 and 142), stopping points whose RGB LED shows their state: free, capsule detected, full.</li>
          <li><b>Radars</b>, standalone and battery-powered, which give the capsules their speed, their direction and an ID.</li>
        </ul>
